// wrangler configuration for the hosted revkit Worker (ADR-0008, M4
// slice 1 / issue #9).
//
// This file is written to be DEPLOYABLE-READY and NOT-YET-DEPLOYED.
// There is no `account_id`, no `routes`, no custom domain and no secret,
// because every one of those is owner-gated (#34) and none of them is
// needed to build, test or run the Worker. `packages/worker/test/`
// asserts that absence rather than trusting this comment.
//
// **`compatibility_flags: []` is load-bearing.** With `nodejs_compat` OFF,
// the platform itself refuses `node:*` imports and does not provide
// `Buffer`, `process` or `require`. That turns ADR-0025's "no Node-only
// deps in the shared core" from a lint into a runtime fact: a regression
// goes red on the FIRST test that touches the affected path, in workerd,
// rather than in production. Measured on miniflare 4.20260518.0 with an
// empty flag list: `typeof Buffer === "undefined"`, same for `process`
// and `require`. That measurement is also why
// `@revkit/review-core/http-headers` encodes CSP hashes without `Buffer`.
//
// `workers_dev: false` is the other load-bearing line, and it is what
// makes slice 1 safe to ship without ADR-0012 authorization. A Worker
// with `workers_dev` left at its default is reachable at
// `*.workers.dev`, so an unauthenticated `GET /api/threads` would be on
// the public internet. With it false and no `routes`, this Worker has NO
// public URL at all until `revkit deploy init` provisions one — which is
// owner-gated (#34) and lands after slice 2's sessions, so there is no
// window in which an unauthorized read is reachable.
//
// `d1_databases[].database_id` is a PLACEHOLDER. Provisioning is
// `wrangler d1 create`, which needs an account, so `revkit deploy init`
// replaces this value with the provisioned id. It is deliberately an
// obvious placeholder rather than a plausible-looking UUID: a fake id
// that reads like a real one would let a deploy fail confusingly later.
// The BINDING NAME is not a placeholder — `env.DB` is what the code binds
// and the test asserts the name.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "revkit-review",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-18",
  "compatibility_flags": [],
  "workers_dev": false,
  "vars": {
    "REVKIT_VERSION": "0.0.0"
  },
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "DB",
      "database_name": "revkit-review",
      "database_id": "PLACEHOLDER_REPLACED_BY_REVKIT_DEPLOY_INIT"
    }
  ]
}
